<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.4 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.4 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 7.4 percent in the week to October 23 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 7.6 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			  Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  20.72	  20.71	     19.28</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	2.02	   1.90		1.84</p>
